---
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >-
    -bugprone-unchecked-optional-access,
    -clang-analyzer-optin.core.EnumCastOutOfRange,
    -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-pointer-arithmetic,
    -cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-vararg,
    -cppcoreguidelines-rvalue-reference-param-not-moved,
    -readability-magic-numbers,

# Reasons for checks disabled in test code (in addition to those disabled in
# the root .clang-tidy):
# bugprone-unchecked-optional-access
#   Cannot see through Catch2's REQUIRE/CHECK macros, so the idiomatic
#   'REQUIRE(o.has_value()); CHECK(o->x());' flags every access (hundreds of
#   false positives).
# clang-analyzer-optin.core.EnumCastOutOfRange
#   Fires inside Catch2 headers (analyzer diagnostics bypass the header
#   filter) and on deliberate out-of-range casts in error-code tests.
# cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-pointer-arithmetic
#   Inherent to shared-memory and message-framing test fixtures that poke at
#   raw buffers.
# cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-vararg
#   Vararg syscalls (fcntl, etc.) are needed in fixtures exercising fds.
# cppcoreguidelines-rvalue-reference-param-not-moved
#   Test lambdas take rvalue references to match continuation signatures but
#   often only inspect the argument.
# readability-magic-numbers
#   Literal values are normal in test data and expectations.
...
